  "sentence_method": "one complete sentence per generation",
  "word_method": "independent word generation, not extracted from sentence audio",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Wetlands are any land that is flooded with shallow water all or most of the time.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-01.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "They are a natural water holding system.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-02.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Many animals come to wetlands to drink water when they are thirsty.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-03.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "There are many types of wetlands.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-04.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Among them, bogs, marshes and swamps are the three main types.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-05.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In bogs, only mosses and a few other kinds of plants can grow.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-06.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "text": "Grassy plants like cattails and reeds are the most common plants in a marsh.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-07.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "text": "A swamp is a forest whose ground is underwater all or most of the time.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-08.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "text": "Unlike bogs or marshes, a swamp is full of trees and bushes, with some trees standing tall as a tower.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-09.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "text": "A special kind of rose also grows here.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-10.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "text": "The swamp is worth a short tour, but you'd better not try without a guide.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-11.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "text": "There are hidden pools of water, thick mud, and sometimes big crocodiles looking for their next meal.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-12.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "text": "Hungry crocodiles aren't the only animals that make the wetlands their home.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-13.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "text": "Otters, turtles, frogs, snakes and many other animals do too.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-14.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "text": "The water is home to many kinds of fish and crabs.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-15.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "text": "Birds, including ducks, geese and cranes, use wetlands seasonally during their long migrations.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-16.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "text": "Wetlands are important because they provide habitats for plants and animals.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-17.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "text": "A wetland system can also protect shorelines, make polluted waters clean, prevent floods and restore underground water supplies.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-18.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "text": "It is important to let the wetlands perform their usual functions.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-19.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "text": "Therefore, many voluntary groups work to protect wetlands by providing different services, such as clean-up events and educating the public.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-20.mp3",
      "exists": true
    }
  ],
